    *   Why would someone delay an upgrade (e.g., software, career move, lifestyle change) because of a busy calendar?
    *   Reason: Cognitive load, lack of time to actually learn the new system, or the "transition tax." If you're already drowning, adding a new variable causes diminishing returns.

    *   *Draft 1:* Often, we rush to upgrade our systems or workflows to be more efficient. But when the calendar is already overflowing, a new upgrade becomes a liability. Every transition requires a steep learning curve and mental bandwidth. If you don't have the breathing room to actually master the new tools, you're just adding stress to an already overloaded plate. Wait until the schedule clears up so you can actually reap the benefits rather than just surviving the implementation phase.

    *   *Word count check:* 82 words.
